From 455d5aa947540c1ad23617a784cddfc2a5c41c5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 07:30:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wip/kv-residency: A4 -- close the spilled-KV purity blocker
 (the VMM host-mapping hazard)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The blocker (A2 §3.7.6): a spilled KV was not numerically transparent -- a
single 4 MiB tensor spill changed the greedy text on a 27B (305 e2cea6fa6670
-> 325 fb65430049e9) and the prefill-logit gate read KLD 0.004973 / 98.761 %.

The flip was never at fault.  Its stage-out equals an INDEPENDENT copy-engine
read of the same mapping, byte for byte, and its restore equals the stage, byte
for byte -- both exhaustively, 32/32 flips, with the old every-512th-byte
compare replaced (that compare was blind to both sides being wrong).

The fault is one level down, in the primitive: `cuMemUnmap` of a device mapping
followed by `cuMemCreate`(HOST)/`cuMemMap` at that VA ZEROES a different, LIVE
host-location mapping in the same reservation.  A 0xAB canary is overwritten, so
it is a real write; a kernel-vs-copy-engine reader cross-check agrees.  The
victims are whole 4 MiB mappings, the mapping flipped one step earlier.
Reproducer: wip/kv-residency/hostmap-hazard-probe.cc (in the delivery repo).

Fix: `vmm_map` holds the physical an imminent unmap released in the runtime
allocator's free list for the duration of its create -- on EVERY map site, not
only the flip, because the hazard is a property of the create that follows a
release.  `LLAMA_KV_REGION_QUARANTINE=0` is the kill-switch (A/B only; the
spill is not transparent with it off).  A refused hold fails the mapping with a
loud message instead of proceeding corrupt.

Gates (all 1 GPU, gfx1201, hardened default):
  27B q8_0 -c 8192, W=1024, n 64 ........ 305 e2cea6fa6670 = plain (kill-switch: 328, wrong)
  27B f16 KV, same shape ................ also corrupted before, identical now
  4B -c 16384 W=1024 (a REAL spill) ..... 26 158c1671e511 = plain   [was 21 9bef5c01369c]
  §6 identity trio, W=2048/4096 spilling  526 5ba44647188f all three
  prefill-logit --ctx 8192 --chunks 4 ... KLD -0.000000 / 100.000 %
  (same arm, QUARANTINE=0 ............... KLD 0.004973 / 98.761 %, the recorded block)
  OOM config, feature off ............... still OOMs (8704.00 MiB)
  VMM selftest / check-gpu-faults ....... PASS / clean

Corrections to the record that this session established, and that the docs keep
getting wrong: the 4B was NOT immune (its arms never reached a flip); the quant
type is not involved (f16 diverges too); the NB1 1088-vs-2048 lead was a red
herring; and the §6 identity trio at W=2048/4096 n 128 is NOT sensitive to this
hazard (it passed while corrupted) -- the sensitive arms are the W=1024 n 64 text
arm and the prefill-logit gate.

Also: the DEBUG instrumentation is now usable -- byte-exhaustive restore verify,
stage-out cross-check, per-host-mapping fingerprint (reports WHERE and WHEN a
spill changes), region dump, canary, and `LLAMA_KV_REGION_TRACE` for every
address-level map/unmap/memset.  LLAMA_KV_REGION_DEBUG is 10-40x on a spilling
arm (it re-reads and hashes every host mapping per growth): never quote a
timing from a DEBUG arm.
